        { "k": "C", "text": "GitHub issues per repo." },
        { "k": "D", "text": "No task lists: keep exactly one next step per project, nothing more." }
      ],
      "rec": { "option": "A", "why": "STATUS.md is already the file every session reads first and updates last, on both machines, so tasks there get maintained as a side effect of normal work. Moving them into portfolio.json (B) gives two places to update and the registry becomes a hot-edited file across machines (merge conflicts). Issues (C) live outside the session routine and would go stale. D is tempting for focus but loses the second and third steps you already write. The cost of A: the PM view has to read ~60 files to show tasks, and Drive-only projects need a small fallback." },
      "status": "open", "durable": true, "updated": false, "thread": []
    }
  ]
}

